        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nFor Sale by DNG Online Auction TO REGISTER FOR OUR ONLINE AUCTION on the 3rd December 2026 at 1pm.Visit www.dngauctions.ieChoose/ Search for your property of interest, click log in & register to bid and follow the necessary steps.Bidder security required prior to auction date in order to successfully bid on the day.DNG Martin O'Connor Land Sales are delighted to offer for sale by DNG Online Auction this fine parcel of grazing land situated at Rusheeny, on the outskirts of Oughterard Village.Contained within Folio GY4010F, File Plan 83 extends to approximately 3.71 Ha (9.16 acres) and comprises a good-sized holding laid out in a number of fields, together with a small area of mountain land situated towards the centre of the property.Access is provided over the old Rusheeny Road which runs along the hillside, while the lands are predominantly enclosed by traditional stone walls.Offering useful grazing in an established agricultural area, this holding should be of particular interest to local farmers and adjoining landowners seeking to increase their existing acreage.\n\nPlease note this property will be offered by online auction (unless sold prior). Vendors may decide to accept pre-auction bids so please register your interest with us to avoid disappointment. The successful bidder is required to pay the balance of 10% deposit and contracts are signed immediately on acceptance of a bid.Directions: From Oughterard village proceed along Main Street towards Clifden passing the Garda Station on your left. Just before the Bridge turn left at McNamaras Shop & the Beauty House salon it will be signposted Costelloe and Shannapheasteen. Drive out this road past the Oughterard Motors and take the next right turn onto the Rusheeny Road. Driving for about half a mile turn left a stone built shed with a green roof directly after Eircode H91H9WX . Go to the next lane after a large Grey Shed and turn left up the hill boreen. The lane is narrow and not suited to a vehicle. Walk along the Boreen following the Map to the DNG Martin O'Connor For Sale Sign identifying the lands."
